@startuml
title MODRISS Continuous-Delivery Iteration Inside Phase 1
skinparam backgroundColor #F5F3ED
skinparam shadowing false
start
repeat
  :Define release outcome hypothesis and scope;
  repeat
  repeat
    :Deliver one bounded vertical model-driven increment;
    :Accept CIM, PIM, PSM, artifacts and G2–G5 evidence;
  repeat while (Another increment needed?) is (yes)
  :Assemble immutable release candidate;
  :Review compatibility, security, quality, cost,\nrecovery and operational readiness at G6;
repeat while (G6 rejected?) is (yes — correct authoritative source)
:Promote progressively;
if (Stop threshold breached?) then (yes)
  :Retain accepted baseline in operation and create corrective work;
else (no)
  :G7 handover to Operations and Maintenance;
endif
if (Retirement authorized?) then (yes)
  :Exit Phase 1 and enter Phase 2;
  :Complete retirement work while Operations independently\nsustains and shuts down remaining live releases;
  :Accept shared G8 closure evidence\nwhen no live release remains;
  stop
else (no)
  :Select roadmap and operational evidence\nfor the next release hypothesis;
endif
repeat while (Next release selected and product active?) is (next release)

legend bottom
  This repeating unit is an Iteration composed of Activities, not a Phase.
  The accepted baseline remains in operation until a later G7 handover.
endlegend
@enduml
